<Task version="1.3" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/windows/2004/02/mit/task">
  <RegistrationInfo>
    <URI>\Hermes-GDrive-Backup</URI>
    <Description>Sauvegarde quotidienne ciblee sur GDrive (mandat user 23/10 : "Absolument tout doit etre backupe sur GDrive", pas de tars de volume entier). Essentials chaque jour : memories, SOUL.md, skills, config.yaml, .env*, cron/jobs.json. Le dimanche (UTC) ajoute state.db compresse, l historique de conversations dont la perte a motive le mandat. Declencheur quotidien 01:53 locale, StartWhenAvailable (rattrapage si la machine dormait). Verifier le LOG roosync-cluster/logs/gdrive-backup.log ET l archive produite, pas seulement LastTaskResult : un code de sortie peut mentir dans les deux sens.</Description>
    <Author>Hermes Agent workspace</Author>
  </RegistrationInfo>
  <Principals>
    <Principal id="Author">
      <!-- TEMPLATE, not registerable as-is: Task Scheduler rejects an empty
           UserId and this repo is a public fork, so no SID is versioned.
           register-host-watchdog.ps1 -Watchdog gdrive-backup substitutes it
           (dry run by default, -Apply to register). -->
      <UserId>__USER_SID__</UserId>
      <LogonType>InteractiveToken</LogonType>
    </Principal>
  </Principals>
  <Settings>
    <DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>true</DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>
    <StopIfGoingOnBatteries>true</StopIfGoingOnBatteries>
    <ExecutionTimeLimit>PT30M</ExecutionTimeLimit>
    <MultipleInstancesPolicy>IgnoreNew</MultipleInstancesPolicy>
    <RestartOnFailure>
      <Count>2</Count>
      <Interval>PT5M</Interval>
    </RestartOnFailure>
    <StartWhenAvailable>true</StartWhenAvailable>
    <IdleSettings>
      <StopOnIdleEnd>false</StopOnIdleEnd>
    </IdleSettings>
    <UseUnifiedSchedulingEngine>true</UseUnifiedSchedulingEngine>
  </Settings>
  <Triggers>
    <!-- CalendarTrigger/DaysInterval=1 = DAILY, NOT a repetition interval (a
         30-minute <Repetition> would turn a daily backup into 48 runs/day).
         The registrar rewrites the StartBoundary to the next 01:53 at install
         time. StartWhenAvailable covers sleep.
         Measured 2026-10-26: this template first shipped a bare <TimeTrigger>,
         which fires ONCE and leaves NextRunTime=null after that single run -
         the 01:53 run happened, tomorrow's would never have. DaysInterval is
         what makes the trigger repeat; a TimeTrigger has none. -->
    <CalendarTrigger>
      <StartBoundary>2026-10-26T01:53:00+01:00</StartBoundary>
      <ScheduleByDay>
        <DaysInterval>1</DaysInterval>
      </ScheduleByDay>
    </CalendarTrigger>
  </Triggers>
  <Actions Context="Author">
    <Exec>
      <Command>wscript.exe</Command>
      <Arguments>//B //Nologo "C:\ProgramData\claude-hidden-launchers\Hermes-GDrive-Backup.vbs"</Arguments>
    </Exec>
  </Actions>
</Task>
